 ## Operating characteristics
-* **Efficiency:** GS-IR achieves real-time rendering efficiency by using 3D Gaussians and forward mapping splatting, contrasting with the high computational complexity of NeRF-based methods [S1]. Exact time and memory complexity metrics are not given in the sources.
-* **Scene Scope:** Unlike TensoIR, which leverages ray tracing of NeRF to directly model occlusion and indirect illumination but is limited to object-level scenes, GS-IR handles occlusion via baking and is available for both objects and unbounded scenes [S1].
-* **Expressiveness:** The flexible and expressive 3DGS representation allows for fast and compact geometry reconstruction [S1].
